### gloss être
to be; to be located, to be situated; to denote time, day, or date; used to form compound tenses and structures, such as the perfect and pluperfect; being, thing, creature; being, the state or fact of existence
### gloss avoir
to have, to own, to possess, to get; to have (to experience or suffer from a state or condition); to have (an age); used to form the compound tenses of most verbs, such as the perfect and pluperfect; to have (to), must; (chiefly in se faire avoir) to have (to trick, to con); asset, possession
### gloss aller
to go; to attend (school, church regularly); to be going (to), will soon, forms a near-future tense; to be (feeling); to go well; to suit; to be X-proof (to be suitable for use in an appliance without running the risk of being damaged in the process); outward trip, journey out, trip away
### gloss faire
to do; to make; to say (of a person), to go (of an animal or device); to make (cause someone or something to do something); to act like (something); to be (of the weather or various situations); to do, to make (oneself); to be, to get (used for a passive action)
### gloss pouvoir
can, to be able to; may (of a choice); to be possible, may, could be; to have the right (to); to have the power, the authority or the talent (to do something); power; authority; power of attorney
### gloss dire
to say, to tell (to express through speech); to tell (to order, to advise); to say, to tell (to set out in writing); to say (often used in the sense of responding to an objection); to say, to tell of (to celebrate, to sing, to narrate); to say, to tell (to deliver, to recite); saying (that which is said); belief, opinion
### gloss venir
to come (to move from one place to another that is nearer the speaker); used in venir de with the meaning of “originate from” or “have just done”; to cum, to come, to orgasm
### gloss prendre
to take; to eat, to drink; to get, to buy; to rob, to deprive; to make; to catch, to work, to start; to get (something) caught (in), to jam; to get into, to come over (to cause to behave uncharacteristically, to affect in a surprising manner, to possess)
### gloss voir
to see (visually); to see (to understand); to see (to visit, to go and see); please (used to mark the imperative)
### gloss vivre
to live; to experience
